<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  FISH_BESTIARY_BUILD_1, wave 5 — the Twilight Deep's fishTypes binding
  (fish_bestiary_commission_2026-09-10.md §2D), the exact file the doc's own
  build sketch names (§5.2: "new ... BiomeFishTypes_TwilightDeep.xml under
  DEPLOY_HOLD.txt").

  ✅ HOLD LIFTED — owner ruling, 2026-09-20, verbatim: "Just make the surface
  fishable." (TWILIGHT_DEEP_WATER_LAYER_1). This drops the "one BiomeDef,
  two water bodies" premise the hold below was built on — there is no
  separate no-fish surface / fishable under-roof split any more; the 8
  Twilight species fish the biome's water via `RUT_TwilightSea`'s own
  `fishTypes`, same as any other fishable biome. The three candidate
  under-roof-water-layer shapes this item once weighed (a pocket-map biome,
  a GravTide petition, shelving the species) are dead, not deferred.

  Superseded history, kept for provenance only: this patch previously sat
  under DEPLOY_HOLD.txt because an earlier ruling read Twilight's surface as
  deliberately no-fish while the deep water beneath it was meant to be
  fishable, and `RUT_TwilightSea` has only ever been one BiomeDef for both.
  That distinction is no longer the design.

  Values: saltwater_Common/_Uncommon exactly as §2D's table; maxFishPopulation
  700 — "high... against the Greentide's 720 as the ceiling, not above it"
  (the doc's own instruction), one economy-size population but not the
  largest on the planet. rareCatchesSetMaker -> RUT_RareTwilightCatches
  (RUT_RareTwilightCatches.xml, sibling, this wave).
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
    <xpath>/Defs/BiomeDef[defName="RUT_TwilightSea"]</xpath>
    <value>
      <maxFishPopulation>700</maxFishPopulation>
      <fishTypes MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">
        <saltwater_Common>
          <RUT_Niim>1.5</RUT_Niim>
          <RUT_Pallu>1</RUT_Pallu>
          <RUT_Tikkarr>0.8</RUT_Tikkarr>
          <RUT_Nuudal>0.6</RUT_Nuudal>
          <RUT_Aluun>0.6</RUT_Aluun>
        </saltwater_Common>
        <saltwater_Uncommon>
          <RUT_Kellu>1</RUT_Kellu>
          <RUT_Murrol>0.8</RUT_Murrol>
          <RUT_Hollu>0.8</RUT_Hollu>
          <RUT_Oobo>0.4</RUT_Oobo>
          <RUT_Liiru>0.5</RUT_Liiru>
        </saltwater_Uncommon>
        <rareCatchesSetMaker>RUT_RareTwilightCatches</rareCatchesSetMaker>
      </fishTypes>
    </value>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
